- **Loading (§6.3):** the loading view now uses the same grid and margins as the loaded view, so nothing jumps when parsing ends.
  - The stage column shows the caption "Reading…" and the bare silicon disc with its shadows. The disc is 596 px at 1440 × 900, the same as the loaded view; I checked this in the browser.
  - The verdict column shows the file name, "Reading records", a 2 px progress track (320 px wide, full width on mobile) and the "4.2 of 9.8 MB" readout.
  - "Reading…" is a new key, added in all 5 locales.
- **Parse error (§6.4, §9.6):** the title uses `title-1`. It is centred at y = 164 from 1024 px and left-aligned at y = 96 below that. There is one filled button, "Open another file", plus a secondary "Open the sample lot" and "Show details" 16 px below. The sample cards stay below.
- **Drag overlay (§6.5):** it now uses the `scrim` token and a 16 px inset frame with 28 px corners and a 1.5 px `hairline-strong` line, for both file and non-file drags. The dot grid is gone. The overlay is now hidden on touch devices rather than on narrow windows.
- **Bins-only (§6.6, §7.16):** the sheet title uses `title-1`, with 28 px before the buttons. "Use bins-only" is the only filled button, is focused, and sits last on the right on desktop. The notice icon now takes the secondary text colour.
- **Shared sheet:** I changed the shared sheet component to the §7.16 surface, shadow, `scrim` backdrop and grabber. This also restyles the error-details sheet, which §7.16 gives the same surface. Its contents are left for P22.

